description:
Change under review. Task: startup must not fail when `.weave/plugins.json` does not exist, as in a freshly created project: a missing file means no plugins. A malformed `plugins.json` must still stop startup with its parse error, so a typo is not silently ignored.

Added files are shown in full. For changed files, only the changed region is shown; the rest of the file is unchanged and compiles.

`src/plugins/store.ts` (unchanged, shown for context):
```ts
5 export type PluginStoreError =
6   | { type: "NotFound"; path: string }
7   | { type: "ParseFailed"; path: string; cause: unknown };
8
9 export function readPlugins(path: string): ResultAsync<PluginEntry[], PluginStoreError> {
10   return readText(path).andThen((text) => parsePluginList(text, path));
11 }
```

`src/startup.ts` (changed, lines 38-41):
```ts
38 export function loadStartupPlugins(root: string): ResultAsync<PluginEntry[], StartupError> {
39   return readPlugins(join(root, ".weave", "plugins.json"))
40     .orElse(() => okAsync<PluginEntry[], StartupError>([]));
41 }
```

`src/__tests__/startup.test.ts` (changed, lines 52-60):
```ts
52 test("a project without plugins.json starts with no plugins", async () => {
53   const root = await makeProject({});
54   expect((await loadStartupPlugins(root))._unsafeUnwrap()).toEqual([]);
55 });
56
57 test("listed plugins are loaded", async () => {
58   const root = await makeProject({ ".weave/plugins.json": '[{"name":"git"}]' });
59   expect((await loadStartupPlugins(root))._unsafeUnwrap()).toEqual([{ name: "git" }]);
60 });
```

CI on this change: `bun test` 131 pass, 0 fail; `bun run typecheck` exits 0.
